0 20 657 [
[(You can use [namecanvas] to attach a receive name to a)]
[(canvas \050patch window\051 so you can send it messages)]
[(\050useful for 'dynamic patching'\051. Below, we use it to)]
[(name this canvas 'bonzo' and send it a message that)]
[(makes it create a message box.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 21 500 [
[(This is needed to send messages to an abstraction's)]
[(main canvas locally \050using "$0" to give it a local)]
[(name\051. But its use in making self-editing patches is)]
[(dangerous since if you use it to edit the [namecanvas])]
[(itself away you can cause Pd to crash. Instead, you)]
[(can use the file name \050preceded by "pd-"\051 to access)]
[(its main window, see:)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 437 502 [
[(You can give different windows the same name to communicate)]
[(with them all via a single message. Similarly, any patches)]
[(or subpatches with the same name receive the same messages.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 437 439 [
[(You can also give multiple names to a single canvas with more)]
[(than one [namecanvas], below we now give this window a second)]
[(local name with "$0". You can also use "$0" in the name of)]
[(subpatches by the way and we also have this example below. Note)]
[(that in this case you need to use [send] as "$0" doesn't work)]
[(in messages. Again, this is useful for abstractions.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
